  "overview": "**DB UI** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#db0016` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `DB Screen Sans` (22px display down to 16px body), unified by `4px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Deutsche Bahn**. Source: published token package (https://db-ui.github.io/core/), package `@db-ui/core`. Inventory: **91** colors, **9** typography steps, and **17** documented components (Apache-2.0 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 17 component tokens with documented paddings: `1rem`, `.375rem .625rem`, `0.375rem 0.625rem`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#fdfdfd` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0 5px rgba(0,0,0,.08),0 5px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.05)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#db0016` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#db0016` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.9:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `DB Screen Sans` headings with `DB Screen Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `4px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#fdfdfd` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `4px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
